      en: "Nieuw Land National Park, established in 2018 in Flevoland, covers 28,000 hectares. It comprises the wetlands of Lepelaarplassen, Oostvaardersplassen, and Marker Wadden. Created on reclaimed land from the IJsselmeer, it is a vital stopover for migratory birds, hosting millions. Known for free-roaming Konik horses and Heck cattle. Visitors can use observation towers and trails. The park represents a unique man-made ecosystem.",
